{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#430","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#430","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#430\",\"parent_revision\":\"da3591e9fb5b73d0c5959be9145bd1ec444c72bf\",\"root_revision\":\"10776a992c6f10fc1aefa4a1714b4a089d53d800ab67ee2c6384174147ac922a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch` skill can be invoked from the plan at the end of `superpowers:executing-plans`, but when `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` is the active execution pattern the finishing step must not run mid-session \u2014 it is only valid after the final code quality reviewer has approved all tasks. The skill currently has no guard against being invoked while subagent-driven-development is still dispatching subagents. A note (and ideally a check) is needed: if a subagent-driven-development session is in progress in the current worktree, warn and refuse to run finishing-a-development-branch until all tasks show complete.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer reading the documentation**, I want to **finishing-a-development-branch: add note that it must not run while subagent-driven-development is in progress in the same worktree** so that **documentation is accurate and trustworthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 executing-plans invoked finishing-a-development-branch without awareness that subagent-driven-development was the active execution pattern\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 The `finishing-a-development-branch` skill can destroy in-progress subagent work if invoked prematurely. The harm is real (orphaned commits, unchecked code, cleanup work wasted) but requires an unusual mistake: a developer or plan invoking the skill mid-session rather than at the end.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: any developer running superpowers:subagent-driven-development who also has an executing-plans-style plan that calls finishing-a-development-branch at the end \u2014 the finish step may fire before the final code quality reviewer approves all tasks.\\n- Bottleneck: missing guard means the only protection is the developer noticing; no automated check exists.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Prevents premature branch cleanup during active subagent dispatch sessions.\\n- Makes the interaction between executing-plans and subagent-driven-development explicit and safe.\\n- Reduces confusion about when finishing-a-development-branch is valid to invoke.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch is invoked, it should detect whether superpowers:subagent-driven-development is still dispatching subagents in the current worktree. If tasks are not all marked complete, the skill should warn the developer and refuse to proceed until all tasks show as complete. This detection is observable: the skill either proceeds or prints a warning and halts.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe finishing-a-development-branch SKILL.md in the obra/superpowers repository contains a guard section (prose note and/or flowchart step) stating: if a subagent-driven-development session is in progress in the current worktree (i.e., not all tasks are complete), warn and refuse to run. The guard is present whether the implementation is documentation-only or also adds a runtime check.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Reading `finishing-a-development-branch/SKILL.md` in the obra/superpowers repo shows a note or guard block stating it must not run while subagent-driven-development is in progress.\\n2. The note or guard specifies the condition: all tasks in the current worktree must be marked complete before finishing-a-development-branch proceeds.\\n3. If a runtime check is included: invoking the skill when tasks are not complete produces a warning and does not proceed to merge/PR/cleanup steps.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | research/agent-frameworks/superpowers.md |\\n| External repo | https://github.com/obra/superpowers (target for change) |\\n| Context source | Session observation: executing-plans invoked finishing-a-development-branch without awareness that subagent-driven-development was active |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: access to the obra/superpowers repository to submit a change (fork or PR)\\n- Blocks: None in this repository\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- The `finishing-a-development-branch` and `subagent-driven-development` SKILL.md files live in the external obra/superpowers repository, which is not installed in the local plugin cache. The implementer must check out or fork obra/superpowers to make the change.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 one SKILL.md file in an external repo; add a prose guard and optionally a flowchart check node. No code changes required unless a runtime state-check mechanism is added.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The skill invocation is valid in one execution context (executing-plans without subagent-driven-development) and invalid in another (when subagent-driven-development is the active pattern). No guard prevents the invalid invocation.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: executing-plans plan calls finishing-a-development-branch while subagent-driven-development is still dispatching, finishing-a-development-branch refuses to run and displays a warning until all tasks are complete\\n\",\"digest\":\"d27e76c0e41bc43597dfbee4052821fc7d7387af42c8ccb027132faa78c83ee8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnNWpg\"}"}